  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $4.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5p+q=3 \\\\ 6p-\\frac{1}{4}q=-8 & |\\,\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}5p+q=3 \\\\ 24p-q=-32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $q$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-q$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $q$-variable, and allows us to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+\\cancel{q} & =3 \\\\ 24p-\\cancel{q} & =-32 \\\\ 29p & =-29 \\\\ p & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $p=-1$ into the equation $5p+q=3$ to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+q & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-1)+q & =3 \\\\ -5+q & =3 \\\\ q & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-1,\\,q=8.$",
